    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3694" root="تأم" body-key="t">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتْأَمَتْ</span></b>  <i>She</i> (a mother, K, or a woman, S,
M, Msb, and any pregnant animal, M) <i>twinned,</i>
or <i>brought forth two at one birth.</i> (T, S, M,
Msb, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتْأَمَهَا</span> <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْضَاهَا</span> [like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آتَمَهَا</span>, q. v.
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتم</span>]. (S, K.) [Golius and Freytag have
rendered it as though it meant <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْضَى إِلَيْهَا</span>.]

